  "landfallEstimate": "Tracking over Bay of Bengal; Doppler radars monitoring",
  "rawBulletin": "REGIONAL SPECIALISED METEOROLOGICAL CENTRE -TROPICAL CYCLONES, NEW DELHI\nTROPICAL CYCLONE ADVISORY NO. 16\nDEMS-RSMC SPECIAL TROPICAL CYCLONES NEW DELHI DATED 03.11.2026\nFROM: RSMC \u2013TROPICAL CYCLONES, NEW DELHI\nTO: STORM WARNING CENTRE, NAYPYITAW (MYANMAR)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, BANGKOK (THAILAND)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, COLOMBO (SRILANKA)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, DHAKA (BANGLADESH)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, KARACHI (PAKISTAN)\nMETEOROLOGICAL OFFICE, MALE (MALDIVES)\nOMAN METEOROLOGICAL DEPARTMENT,\nMUSCAT (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nYEMEN METEOROLOGICAL SERVICES,\nREPUBLIC OF YEMEN (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nNATIONAL CENTRE FOR METEOROLOGY, UAE (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nPRESIDENCY OF METEOROLOGY AND ENVIRONMENT,\nSAUDI ARABIA (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nIRAN METEOROLOGICAL ORGANISATION, (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nQATAR METEOROLOGICAL DEPARTMENT (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nTROPICAL CYCLONE ADVISORY NO. 16 FOR NORTH INDIAN OCEAN (THE BAY OF\nBENGAL AND ARABIAN SEA) ISSUED AT 0800 UTC OF 03.11.2026 BASED ON 0600 UTC\nOF 03.11.2026\nSub: - Severe Cyclonic Storm \u201cMurasu\u201d [Pronunciation: Murasu] over South Coastal Andhra\nPradesh.\nThe Severe Cyclonic Storm \u201cMurasu\u201d [Pronunciation: Murasu]\u201d over south coastal Andhra Pradesh\nmoved north-northwestwards with a speed of 06 kmph during past 06 hours and lay centered at 0600 UTC\nof today the 03rd November, 2026 over the same region, near Latitude 15.9\u00b0N and Longitude 80.1\u00b0E\nabout 40 km west of Bapatla (Andhra Pradesh), 50 km north of Ongole, 90 km southwest of Vijayawada\n(Andhra Pradesh), 110 km north of Kavali (Andhra Pradesh) and 120 km west-southwest of Machilipatnam\n(Andhra Pradesh).\nThe maximum sustained windspeed was 85-95 gusting to 105 kmph at 0600 UTC of today, the 3rd\nNovember 2026.\nThe Severe Cyclonic Storm is very likely to continue to move further north-northwestwards and weaken\ngradually into a cyclonic storm (wind speed reaching 80-90 kmph gusting to 100 kmph) by 0900 UTC and\nfurther into a deep depression (wind speed reaching 55-65 kmph gusting to 75 kmph) by 1800 UTC of\ntoday, the 3rd November,2026.\nIt is under the continuous surveillance of Doppler Weather Radars at Machilipatnam and Visakhapatnam.\nCloud distribution: (a) Isolated: <25%, Scattered:25-50%, Broken: 51-75%, Solid:>75%, Convection Intensity: (a) Weak: Cloud Top Temperature(CTT)>-\n25\u00b0C, (b) Moderate: CTT:-25\u00b0Cto-40\u00b0C, (c) Intense: CTT: -41\u00b0Cto -70\u00b0C and (d) Very Intense::Less than -70\u00b0C Probability of cyclogenesis (formation of\ndepression) :NIL:0%, LOW:1-33%, MODERATE:34-66% and HIGH:67-100%\nThis is a guidance Bulletin for WMO/ESCAP Panel Member countries. Visit respective National websites for Country specific Bulletins.\nForecast location and intensity are given in following table:\nDate/Time Position Maximum sustained surface Category of cyclonic\n(UTC) (Lat. 0N/ long. 0E) wind speed (Kmph) disturbance\n03.11.26/0600 15.9/80.1 85-95 gusting to 105 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n03.11.26/1200 16.2/80.0 65-75 gusting to 85 Cyclonic Storm\n03.11.26/1800 16.5/80.0 55-65 gusting to 75 Deep Depression\n04.11.26/0000 16.8/80.0 40-50 gusting to 60 Depression\nThe estimated central pressure is 996.0 hPa and maximum sustained wind speed is 55 kt\ngusting to 65kt.\nVijayawada (43181, Andhra Pradesh) reported mean sea level (MSLP) of 1013.3 hPa, 24 hours\npressure change (P24) as -0.8 hPa and maximum sustained wind speed (MSW) as 500/08kt,\nAmaravati (43176, Andhra Pradesh) reported MSLP of 1011.6 hPa, P24 as -2.4 hPa and MSW\n500/12kt, Bapatla (43220, Andhra Pradesh) reported MSLP of 1007.3 hPa, P24 as -5.3 hPa and\nMSW 1400/14kt, Ongole (43221, Andhra Pradesh) reported MSLP of 1008.6 hPa, P24 as -3.3 hPa\nand MSW 2000/11kt.\nAs per latest INSAT 3DS imagery based on 0600 UTC, Vortex (Murasu) over Coastal Andhra\nPradesh & adjoining West-central Bay of Bengal and neighbourhood. Associated scattered to\nbroken low and medium clouds with embedded intense to very intense convection lay over west\nBay of Bengal, Coastal Andhra Pradesh, Rayalaseema, Telangana, South Chhattisgarh, South\nOdisha and North Tam",
